<title>USA: Taiwan Semiconductor president resigns.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Semiconductor president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co Ltd on Tuesday said its president Don Brooks was resigning effective May 1.</p>
<p>The company said Chairman and Chief Executive Morris Chang would take on the additional position of president.</p>
<p>Brooks said he planned to return to the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;I faced a choice between another long-term commitment in Taiwan as the company comes out of this downturn, continues its aggressive expansion and embraces the rapid pace of technology change,&quot; Brooks said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;On the other side of it, my wife and I left behind friends, children, grandchildren and extended family who we'd like to be closer to.&quot;</p>
</text>
